# Time Display Example

Displays the current system time using the `CurrentTimeNode` connected to visual display nodes.

## Nodes Used

- `system/info/currentTime` — outputs formatted time string and numeric timestamp
- `output/display/text` — shows the time string inline in the node body
- `output/display/number` — shows the timestamp inline in the node body

## Graph

1. Add a `CurrentTimeNode` (System → Info)
2. Add a `TextDisplay` node (Output → Value)
3. Add a `NumberDisplay` node (Output → Value)
4. Connect `CurrentTimeNode.time` → `TextDisplay.text`
5. Connect `CurrentTimeNode.timestamp` → `NumberDisplay.value`

## Pre-made Graph

Import `time-display.json` via the File menu to load the wired graph instantly.

## Build & Run

```bash
cmake --build --preset debug
./build/debug/examples/time-display/TimeDisplayApp
```
